.TH ESL-ANALYZE 1 "March 2026" "ecoSignalLab 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
esl-analyze \- analyze one audio file with ecoSignalLab
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B esl analyze
.I input
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run metric extraction for a single input file and export machine-readable
artifacts plus optional plots and ML outputs.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fIPATH\fR
Write result JSON.
.TP
\fB\-\-csv\fR \fIPATH\fR
Write summary CSV.
.TP
\fB\-\-parquet\fR \fIPATH\fR
Write summary Parquet.
.TP
\fB\-\-hdf5\fR \fIPATH\fR
Write HDF5 export.
.TP
\fB\-\-mat\fR \fIPATH\fR
Write MATLAB .mat export.
.TP
\fB\-\-calibration\fR \fIPATH\fR
Calibration YAML/JSON file.
.TP
\fB\-\-metrics\fR \fILIST\fR
Comma-separated metric IDs.
.TP
\fB\-\-plot\fR
Generate static plots.
.TP
\fB\-\-interactive\fR
Generate interactive Plotly output.
.TP
\fB\-\-similarity-matrix\fR
Generate similarity matrix plot.
.TP
\fB\-\-novelty-matrix\fR
Generate novelty matrix plot.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbosity\fR \fI0..3\fR
Verbosity level.
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR \fI0..2\fR
Debug level.
.SH EXAMPLE
.B esl analyze input.wav --out-dir out --json out/input.json --csv out/input.csv --plot
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR esl (1)
